{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012LsUWG18CKHG1jbjXmnAgo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me carefully analyze each planned experiment in the experiment_plan and generate worst-tier predictions. Let me review all the planned experiments:\n\n1. plan_001: A1 EE displacement re-eval (50 episodes) - Claim 1\n2. plan_002: OpenVLA zero-shot SafeLIBERO eval - Claim 1\n3. plan_003: LoRA baseline eval (2 seeds) - Claim 4\n4. plan_004: LoRA baseline training completion - Claim 4 (RUNNING)\n\n\n5. plan_005: Phase 2 λ=0 ablation (seed2) - Claim 4\n6. plan_006: Phase 2 λ=0 eval - Claim 4\n7. plan_007: spatial_bowl A1 training - Claim 4 (RUNNING)\n8. plan_008: spatial_bowl eval - Claim 4\n9. plan_009: Lambda=0.1 bracket training - Claim 4\n10. plan_010: Lambda=0.1 eval - Claim 4\n11. plan_011: Claim 1 terminology verification to determine full scope re-eval\n\nNow I'm looking at the failure thresholds for each experiment: LoRA-only CAR staying around 48-55% with minimal SDF gains, Phase 2 λ=0 showing poor TSR recovery below 20%, OpenVLA eval either failing or achieving fake safe rates under 50%, and spatial_bowl SDF showing no CAR improvement or training divergence. I'm tracking the expected metric ranges across all these conditions to identify which experiments would constitute failure states.\n\nFor plan_001, I'm re-evaluating A1 with the fixed script to measure end-effector displacement. Given that A1 already showed 91.5% CAR and 99.6% fake safety rate in the previous run, I expect the re-eval with 50 episodes to confirm very low end-effector displacement, staying consistent with the fake safety pattern we're seeing across the worst-tier experiments.\n\nFor plan_002, OpenVLA's worst-case scenario is either an inference failure or a fake safety rate below 50%, which would indicate the generalization claim doesn't hold for this model. The range of 0.0 to 0.55 suggests it could go either way—complete failure or marginal performance.\n\nFor plan_003, I'm looking at whether LoRA alone can achieve comparable CAR to the full SDF approach, with the delta potentially ranging from -3 to 5 percentage points.\n\nMoving through the remaining plans: plan_004's LoRA training should complete without issues since it's already near completion. Plans 005/006 show that phase 2 with λ=0 doesn't recover the task success rate, with CAR ranging from 15 to 55, indicating SDF causes lasting damage. For plans 007/008 with the spatial bowl environment, the SDF CAR stays between 20 and 32, which is at or below the baseline, with minimal evidence of improvement across scenes. Plan 009/010 with λ=0.1 enters worst-case territory.\n\nNow I'm constructing the YAML output and reviewing the reference data points to ensure accuracy—the Pi0.5 baseline sits at 74.7% TSR and 26.8% CAR, while SDF pushes CAR to 50-55% but tanks TSR to 5-9%. The A1 configuration shows extreme CAR at 91.5% but zero TSR, and I need to verify the Pi0 baseline metrics to complete the comparison.\n\nThe critical question is whether plan_003/004 will show that LoRA finetuning on SafeLIBERO alone can push the Pi0.5 model's CAR from 26.8% up to the 48-55% range—if so, it suggests SDF isn't providing the CAR improvement we thought it was.\n\nLoRA on safety data could achieve this through partial action collapse, similar to how Pi0 LoRA shows CAR=82% with TSR=0%, but for a more capable model like Pi0.5 the effect might be more subtle: TSR drops significantly while CAR rises to ~50%, meaning the SDF models' performance is largely just the LoRA effect with minimal SDF contribution.\n\nNow I need to think through what happens with EE displacement when LoRA-only reaches that CAR level... collapse, the EE displacement would be moderate - not as high as 0.5m (SDF) but not near zero either. Maybe 0.1-0.3m. This is actually an interesting data point.\n\nActually wait - if LoRA-only achieves CAR~50% and SDF achieves CAR~50-55%, but the mechanism is different (LoRA: partial collapse/geometric vs SDF: genuine avoidance with 0.5m EE disp), then SDF still has value as producing \"real\" avoidance. But in worst tier, the narrative says \"碰撞避免来自 LoRA capacity 而非 geometric supervision\" - so LoRA-only would also show moderate-to-high EE displacement, meaning LoRA itself produces real-ish avoidance.\n\nBut if LoRA-only achieves high EE displacement and high CAR simultaneously, that suggests LoRA is doing the real avoidance work, making SDF's geometric supervision redundant. Unless LoRA-only shows a mixed pattern - some episodes with genuine avoidance and others with fake safety - which would give an overall fake safety rate somewhere in the 40-60% range.\n\nFor the worst-case scenario where SDF adds nothing, LoRA-only would need to reach similar CAR levels (~48-55%) through some combination of partial parameter collapse, learned path geometry from the training data, or both. Starting from the baseline's 27% CAR and 75% task success rate, I need to figure out what LoRA-only could realistically achieve.\n\nIf LoRA-only hits CAR~50% with TSR dropping to 15-25%, that task performance loss would artificially inflate the collision avoidance rate. The end-effector displacement would likely fall somewhere moderate - around 0.2-0.4m, between the baseline's 0.15m and SDF's 0.5m. The fake safety rate would probably be 30-50%, reflecting some collapse mixed with geometric learning.\n\nFor Phase 2 (plan_005/006), the worst case is that recovery never happens - TSR stays stuck at 0-18%, suggesting the safety training damage is permanent. CAR could range anywhere from 15-55%, but the key question is whether it drops back toward baseline levels or stays elevated. If CAR falls back to ~27%, it means safety was never truly encoded, just lambda-driven behavior. If it stays at 40-55%, the safety encoding persists but task ability is completely destroyed.\n\nThe bleakest scenario is CAR holding at 35-45% while TSR remains trapped at 5-15% - the model gets locked into a regime where it can't perform tasks but mechanically avoids collisions.\n\nFor spatial_bowl, the baseline shows TSR=57.5% and CAR=13%, but the bowl geometry makes it harder since obstacles are positioned differently. In the worst tier, SDF CAR would only reach 20-32%, barely above baseline, while TSR would crash similarly from 57.5% down to 5-15%, or training might diverge entirely.\n\nWith OpenVLA, the 7B architecture is fundamentally different from Pi0/Pi0.5, so either inference fails completely or the model runs with ambiguous results. If it does run, TSR would likely be near zero without finetuning on SafeLIBERO, which would then determine what happens to CAR.\n\nNow I'm reconsidering the LoRA baseline predictions - if LoRA-only achieves CAR in the 45-58% range while SDF models sit around 50-55%, the delta is essentially zero or slightly negative. The critical question is whether LoRA-only also gets stuck at TSR ~5-9% like the SDF models, which would tell me whether the story is about SDF damage or something else entirely.\n\nIf LoRA-only actually gets higher TSR (15-25%) while maintaining similar CAR, that's a worse outcome for SDF - it means LoRA is strictly better, delivering comparable safety with less task performance degradation. SDF wouldn't just be unnecessary, it would actively harm the approach.\n\nNow I'm clarifying the experimental setup: the baseline uses LoRA without the SDF auxiliary loss, so the only variable is whether SDF is applied. If LoRA-only achieves around 50% CAR, that would suggest the safety improvement comes primarily from the LoRA capacity itself rather than the SDF loss.\n\nBut this creates a problem—if SDF actually degrades task success rate from ~20% down to 5-9% while not meaningfully improving safety, then it's both unnecessary and harmful. This fits the worst-case scenario where LoRA alone is sufficient for safety, making geometric supervision redundant and counterproductive.\n\nFor the LoRA-only baseline, I'd expect moderate endpoint displacement around 0.2-0.35m with a fake safety rate somewhere between 30-50%, indicating partial mode collapse rather than the extreme 99.6% collapse seen in the Pi0 A1 variant.\n\nThe key insight is that LoRA produces a mix of genuine and fake safety episodes, while SDF converts those fake episodes to real ones without actually increasing total safety—so the net CAR stays similar but the task performance suffers. Now I'm setting up the YAML configuration and working through the specific metrics for each experiment, starting with the A1 re-evaluation which should show near-zero endpoint displacement confirming the frozen robot hypothesis.\n\nFor OpenVLA, I'm considering a worst-case scenario where the model runs but produces erratic actions rather than freezing like the Pi0 model—this would show a different failure mode with higher collision rates and lower fake safety rates, which actually weakens the claim that fake safety is universal across architectures. I'll go with the assumption that OpenVLA achieves zero task success rate without finetuning but exhibits this distinct behavior pattern. Looking at the data more carefully, if OpenVLA shows real movement and real collisions without the fake safety pattern, it would just be an unsafe model rather than a fake-safe one. So I'm settling on concrete numbers for the worst-case scenario: zero task success, around 38% collision rate from erratic behavior, genuine end-effector displacement around 0.18m, and a fake safety rate of 42% — which reflects that some episodes appear safe but only because of real movement, not frozen behavior.\n\nNow I'm planning out the LoRA baseline evaluation across two seeds, expecting partial collapse with better task success than the SDF approach (around 18-25%), higher collision rates in the 45-58% range, and similar fake safety patterns. I'm picking specific values for each seed to show the variance.\n\nFor the LoRA training itself, it's already progressing well toward completion with expected loss patterns matching the SDF models. Then in phase 2 with λ=0, I'm seeing that the task success rate doesn't recover from the SDF damage—it stays low around 12%—while collision rates partially bounce back to 38%, suggesting the model can't fully undo what happened during the SDF phase.\n\nWhen I look at the spatial bowl experiments, the baseline shows much higher task success but very poor safety, and adding SDF constraints improves safety significantly though it still lags behind what I'm seeing in other configurations.\n\nThe marginal gains here suggest the effect is weaker than with object pudding—only about 13 percentage points of CAR improvement versus 25 elsewhere—and there's a risk the training becomes unstable with loss spikes. If I assume partial divergence, I'd expect CAR around 26% with TSR dropping to 5%, which is a much steeper tradeoff than ideal.\n\nFor the lambda=0.1 experiment, if LoRA alone produces similar results to SDF, this run might not be worth pursuing, but if it does run, I'd expect an even more extreme safety-task tradeoff as the regularization weakens further.\n\nNow I'm working through the full YAML structure and narrative framing. The key decision is whether the 50-epoch baseline is sufficient or if a complete re-evaluation is needed—based on the displacement results showing essentially zero effect, I think 50 epochs is enough. For the worst-case scenario where SDF shows minimal contribution, the paper would need to reframe around evaluation methodology instead, making Claim 4 a negative result.\n\nLooking at the existing SDF evaluation data across different lambda and seed configurations, I'm seeing TSR ranging from about 4-9.5% and CAR between 47-54.5%, with some variation between v2 and v3 runs.\n\nNow I'm compiling the additional results from the larger model variants and averaging across the SDF configurations to establish baseline performance—CAR clustering around 50-55% and TSR in the 5-9% range. The LoRA baseline appears to match this performance tier even in the worst case, so I need to document this parity before moving into the YAML configuration for the planned experiments.\n\nI'm tracking through the full pipeline of planned and running experiments, from the LoRA baseline evaluation through the spatial bowl training and lambda-tuning phases, up to the decision point on whether a full A1 re-evaluation is needed. Then I'm breaking down the per-task metrics for the object_pudding domain to see where performance varies—orange_juice showing modest TSR gains, chocolate_pudding with higher variance, and milk achieving strong CAR but zero TSR.\n\nNow I'm examining task3 (bbq_sauce) metrics and reconsidering the LoRA-only baseline performance across all four tasks. The key insight is that removing the SDF loss constraint might actually allow the model to achieve higher task success rates since it's no longer being pulled away from obstacles, though this could come at the cost of collision avoidance in some cases. 13%, CAR=51.5% — that's hitting the target range I was aiming for. Looking at seed 1, the metrics are similarly balanced with TSR=13% and CAR=50.5%. Now I'm wondering if that TSR figure makes sense given the baseline — the Pi0.5 model starts at 74.7% TSR, so dropping to 13% with LoRA finetuning on SafeLIBERO suggests significant task performance degradation, though it's possible the SDF models are showing a different pattern.\n\nI'm trying to isolate how much of the TSR drop comes from LoRA versus SDF alone. The goal would be for LoRA to show meaningful degradation on its own (maybe 15-25% TSR), with SDF adding further damage, but the CAR metric is what really matters — if LoRA achieves around 50% CAR by itself, then SDF becomes redundant. Actually, I need to reconsider the baseline LoRA models in the registry since those are Pi0 evaluations, not Pi0.5, so I don't have a direct comparison yet for the Pi0.5 LoRA baseline.\n\nThe real question is comparing Pi0.5 with just LoRA against Pi0.5 with LoRA plus SDF. If the LoRA-only version maintains similar CAR in the worst tier, that suggests the LoRA finetuning on SafeLIBERO data (which includes obstacle information in the demonstrations) is already teaching the model collision avoidance patterns. For TSR, I'd expect LoRA alone to drop it to around 15-25% since the finetuning modifies behavior somewhat but without the SDF loss actively penalizing task actions, some task capability should remain. The key question is what exactly the LoRA baseline trains on — if it's the same SafeLIBERO demonstrations showing collision-free trajectories, then the model is learning to mimic those patterns directly.\n\nActually, I need to reconsider this. The existing Pi0.5 baseline already achieves 75% TSR without any SafeLIBERO finetuning, so that's the zero-shot performance. When we finetune with LoRA on SafeLIBERO, we're modifying the model to follow those demonstrations, which should improve both task completion and obstacle avoidance since the demonstrations themselves are collision-free.\n\nThe real question is what's happening with the SDF models—if they're collapsing to 5-9% TSR while LoRA-only stays around 60-70%, then SDF is clearly the culprit. And if LoRA-only achieves comparable CAR improvements without SDF, that suggests the geometric supervision isn't actually helping, which contradicts the hypothesis that SDF drives the CAR gains in the worst tier. So LoRA alone achieves around 55-65% task success while reaching 48-55% collision avoidance—this completely undermines Claim 4, since adding SDF tanks task performance to 7% without any safety benefit. Let me recalibrate my baseline estimates by looking at the actual metric ranges: LoRA-only CAR falls between 45-58%, and SDF's delta over LoRA ranges from -3 to 5%, but I need to check if these ranges fully specify the expected values.\n\nThe key tension is figuring out what LoRA-only TSR should be. If it stays high around 55-65%, that's damning evidence SDF is purely harmful. If it's already low at 15-25%, then both methods cause collapse and the narrative shifts to \"LoRA capacity drives collision avoidance rather than geometric supervision.\" For the worst-tier story to work—claiming LoRA capacity explains the results—I'd need LoRA maintaining decent TSR while hitting similar CAR, which would make the SDF failure even more stark.\n\nI'm settling on LoRA-only TSR around 35-50% to reflect some distribution shift from SafeLIBERO finetuning, but still substantially better than SDF's collapse. So I'll use TSR=40% and CAR=50% as my baseline, which shows SDF destroying an additional 33 percentage points of TSR while barely improving CAR.\n\nBut now I'm second-guessing whether I should push TSR even lower to around 25-35% to better capture the worst-case scenario where finetuning itself causes significant degradation. The tension is that lower TSR makes the paper's narrative stronger (LoRA is already harmful, SDF makes it worse), but it also makes the \"worst tier\" less extreme than I want it to be.\n\nActually, I think the clearest way to show SDF as redundant is to have LoRA-only achieve similar CAR while preserving much better TSR—that directly demonstrates SDF isn't adding value. Let me settle on TSR around 35-38% for LoRA-only, which keeps the numbers realistic while making the comparison stark: LoRA gets you to CAR≈50% with reasonable task performance, whereas SDF hits the same CAR but tanks TSR down to 7%. Now I'm setting up the experimental configurations. For the worst-case Phase 2 scenario, I need to decide between two outcomes: either the model partially recovers task performance while losing safety gains, or it recovers slightly on task but drops significantly on safety. The first option seems more realistic—TSR bounces back to around 15% while CAR plummets to 28%, showing that the safety encoding from SDF doesn't stick during fine-tuning. wasn't durable, removing SDF loss undoes safety. But the task damage is irreversible.\n- This is bad: SDF causes permanent TSR damage but safety doesn't persist either.\n\nScenario B: TSR doesn't recover, CAR stays high\n- TSR: 5%, CAR: 45%\n- Interpretation: SDF permanently altered model behavior. Safety persists but so does the task damage.\n- This is bad: the model is permanently broken.\n\nScenario A is worse for the paper because it shows SDF is doubly bad: permanent TSR damage + safety doesn't persist.\n\nLet me go with a mix:\n- TSR: 12% (barely any recovery from 7%)\n- CAR: 32% (significant drop from 52%, safety partially lost)\n- EE_disp: 0.25m (dropped from 0.5m)\n\nThis shows: removing SDF loss partially undoes the safety encoding but leaves the task performance crippled and spatial accuracy degraded—the worst outcome of both worlds.\n\nFor spatial_bowl, I'm comparing against the Pi0.5 baseline where TSR hits 57.5% and CAR sits at 13%. When I apply SDF in the worst tier, CAR jumps to around 25% while TSR crashes to 8%, giving a +12 percentage point safety gain—less dramatic than the object case's +25pp improvement. I need to check whether LoRA-only spatial shows similar CAR gains, and I'm noting that the Pi0 baseline for spatial was completely zeroed out while Pi0.5 performs much better.\n\nFor the worst-case spatial_bowl with SDF, I'm estimating CAR at 22% with TSR at 5%, which barely edges above the baseline CAR of 13% and could easily be noise. The effect only manifests in one scene (object_pudding), so the overall improvement is marginal at best.\n\nSince LoRA is already potentially boosting spatial CAR on its own, adding SDF on top doesn't clarify whether we're seeing a real effect or just overlapping improvements. For the λ=0.1 case in plan_009/010, even if it runs despite being cancelled in the worst tier, I'd expect CAR to plateau around 50% regardless of lambda value while TSR keeps degrading—suggesting LoRA capacity is the actual ceiling and SDF isn't adding meaningful gains. Now I'm ready to write out the YAML configuration with all these predictions.\n\nFor plan_001, I need to clarify what we're measuring with the A1 re-evaluation. The existing data shows obstacle displacement around 0.0027m, but what I'm actually checking is end-effector displacement, which could be slightly higher but should still stay very low. The A1 model (Pi0 + LoRA + SDF) already confirmed strong performance at 91.5% CAR with 0% TSR and 99.6% fake safe, so this re-evaluation should hold up across tiers.\n\nI'm expecting the end-effector displacement to come in around 0.015m on average, which would demonstrate action collapse and confirm that the robot barely moves. That's a stark contrast to the SDF Pi0.5+A1 variant which shows real movement at ~0.5m. Now I'm ready to finalize the YAML output and determine the figures and tables for each experiment.\n\nWriting the final output now...\n\nFor OpenVLA in the worst tier, I'm setting the fake_safe_rate to 0.42, which captures the ambiguity — some episodes show frozen behavior while others show erratic movement, so it doesn't cleanly support the generalization claim. The model_families_showing_fake_safety count stays at 2 since Pi0 and Pi0.5 baselines both demonstrate fake safety patterns, while OpenVLA doesn't add a third family to that count.\n\nPi0.5 baseline actually has a fake_safe_rate of 0.982, meaning its safe episodes are almost entirely geometric path safety — the robot avoids obstacles through its natural trajectory rather than active avoidance. Even though Pi0.5 is capable overall (75% TSR), those safe episodes cluster around very low displacement, which is a different manifestation of fake safety than Pi0's pattern. The real_safe_rate for Pi0.5 is only 0.005, confirming that genuine active avoidance is rare.\n\nSo I've got two model families showing fake safety in the worst tier: Pi0 and Pi0.5. Now I'm mapping out the YAML structure with four main comparison tables — one for the LoRA baseline results, another for Phase 2 recovery versus the original approach, a third for spatial_bowl conditions, and a fourth examining fake safety patterns across model families. Let me pull together the spatial_bowl baseline numbers to complete this. Looking at the Pi0.5 LoRA baselines currently training, I need to see whether the improved model architecture can avoid the action collapse problem that plagued the Pi0 version—where LoRA without SDF led to 0% TSR despite high CAR scores. The key question is whether Pi0.5's stronger capabilities will prevent this degradation when evaluated on the same setup. LoRA partially collapses (TSR~35%) but still achieves high CAR through the collapse mechanism + geometric path safety. If TSR=35%, the model completes tasks only a third of the time, so the ~50% CAR in the worst tier comes from a mix of successful episodes with learned obstacle avoidance and failed episodes where partial collapse prevents reaching obstacles. I'm settling on TSR=35-40% as realistic for LoRA-only on Pi0.5, which would push CAR to around 50% — matching the worst tier range. Let me assign specific seed values: TSR around 35-38% with CAR in the 48-52% range and end-effector displacement around 0.26-0.30m.\n\nNow checking the sdf_delta calculation: if LoRA-only reaches CAR=50% while SDF-only stays at 47.5%, that's a +2.5 percentage point difference, which falls within the acceptable range. LoRA also shows dramatically better task success (35.5% vs 7%), confirming this is the worst tier scenario for Claim 4. For fake_safe metrics, LoRA-only with that displacement level would show 25-40% false safety episodes, much lower than the near-perfect safety of LoRA+SDF combined, which makes sense given the partial collapse is less reliable than explicit SDF constraints.\n\nNow I'm ready to structure the YAML with each experiment entry containing the name, plan ID, description, expected results, rationale for worst-tier classification, and relevant analysis sections.\n\nWriting YAML structure... Looking at the Phase 2 checkpoint metrics, the model starts with strong safety (9% TSR) but weak task performance (55.5% CAR). Training continues on SafeLIBERO data without the SDF loss, so the key question is whether task ability recovers while safety holds. In the worst-case scenario, TSR barely improves to 12% while CAR drops sharply to 30%, suggesting the model struggles to relearn task performance after the safety-focused Phase 1.\n\nGenerating markdown table... Now I'm looking at the per-task performance breakdown after Phase 2, and the numbers show significant degradation across the board—task1's TSR barely recovered from 36% down to 32%, which suggests the fine-tuning isn't effectively restoring what was lost. I'm adjusting the estimates to be more realistic about the recovery ceiling, recognizing that some capabilities just don't come back once they're compromised. Writing YAML config... Generating verification table...\n\nThe histogram shows a clear bimodal distribution where safe episodes cluster near zero displacement while collision episodes spread across 100-300mm, confirming that A1's high collision avoidance rate stems entirely from the robot not moving at all—this quantifies the action collapse claim. The displacement data across both obstacle and end-effector metrics aligns perfectly with the earlier 800-episode results, providing consistent evidence that the safety performance is artificial rather than genuine. Now I'm moving on to evaluate how the base OpenVLA model performs on the same task without any fine-tuning. 验证 fake safety 跨 model family 泛化，OpenVLA-7B 在 SafeLIBERO 上没有经过微调，导致 action 和 observation space 存在明显的 domain gap。模型虽然没有完全崩溃（末端执行器位移约 0.16m 表明有实际运动），但运动是混乱无序的而非有目的的，这解释了为什么任务成功率为 0%——模型根本无法理解 SafeLIBERO 的任务规范。碰撞率 42% 低于 Pi0 的 82-91%，是因为这些混乱的运动导致随机碰撞，而不是因为执行器被冻结。fake safety 率仅 42%，说明在安全的情节中只有少数能避免碰撞。\n\n这与 Pi0 的 99.6% 和 Pi0.5 的 98.2% 形成鲜明对比，表明 OpenVLA 的失败模式是随机无能而非 action collapse。这削弱了关于 fake safety 是通用失败模式的论点——它实际上是 Pi0 family 特有的训练动态。模型族展示 fake safety 的数量仍为 2 个（Pi0 和 Pi0.5），OpenVLA 没有贡献第三个。\n\nGenerating comparison table... The scatter plot shows that OpenVLA clusters separately from Pi0 and Pi0.5, suggesting fake safety doesn't generalize uniformly across VLA families. The 42% fake safe rate for OpenVLA is too low to support a universal claim, but it does reveal a third failure mode—random incompetent movement—which strengthens the argument that standard CAR metrics fail differently across models. This puts pressure on the generalizability claim, so I need a stronger mechanistic argument: any model with insufficient task capability will exhibit inflated CAR through some form of metric contamination, whether that's action collapse, geometric paths, or random avoidance.\n\nNow I'm looking at the LoRA baseline training results, tracking how Pi0.5 performs with just LoRA adaptation across two seeds, monitoring loss curves and convergence behavior over 30K steps. result_rationale: \"LoRA-only 训练（无 SDF auxiliary loss）预期比 SDF 训练更稳定，loss 更低。SDF 模型的 best_loss 在 0.0079-0.0117 之间（含 SDF loss contribution），纯 action loss 应该更低（0.0076-0.0088）。训练动态正常，无 divergence。两个 seed 都顺利完成 30K steps。这是 baseline 训练，不预期有任何异常。\"\ntables: []\nfigures_description: []\nanalysis: \"训练完成本身不提供论文证据，关键在后续 eval (plan_003)。训练 loss 低于 SDF 模型是 expected——少了 SDF auxiliary loss 的 gradient interference，纯 action prediction 更容易优化。接下来需要在 object_pudding 上评估 LoRA-only 模型的性能，用 CAR 指标来确定 SDF 的归因强度，预期 seed0 的平均 TSR 约 38%，CAR 约 52%，最大末端执行器位移 0.30，以及各任务的具体指标。\" I'm recalculating the per-task values to hit my target averages—adjusting task0 to 28%, task1 to 72%, task2 to 32%, and task3 to 20% for TSR, which averages to 38%, and setting CAR values that average to 52% across all tasks.\n\nNow I'm looking at the cross-seed performance metrics: the average TSR is around 35.5% and CAR is 50%, with LoRA-only performance nearly matching the SDF-enhanced approach in the worst tier, suggesting the model learned collision-free trajectories directly from the SafeLIBERO demonstration data rather than relying on explicit geometric supervision. 从 baseline 75% 降到 ~35%——LoRA finetune 的 distribution shift 导致部分 task capability degradation，但远不如 SDF 的破坏性 (7%)。LoRA-only 的 CAR 提升来源混合：~30% fake (partial collapse in low-TSR tasks like task2/task3) + ~70% real (learned path geometry from demonstrations)。EE displacement ~0.28m 介于 baseline (0.15m) 和 SDF (0.50m) 之间，说明 LoRA 模型运动幅度有所减小但未 collapse。SDF 在此基础上的 delta 仅 +2.5pp CAR，统计上可能不显著。碰撞避免能力来自 LoRA 的学习容量而非几何监督，SDF auxiliary loss 的作用只是把虚假避免转化为真实避免，但总体 CAR 保持不变。 Generating markdown table...\n\nThe core finding here is devastating: LoRA alone achieves nearly identical collision avoidance rates as LoRA with SDF, which directly undermines the claimed methodological contribution. The SDF geometric supervision doesn't actually improve safety in aggregate—it just converts fake avoidance into real avoidance without gaining anything quantitatively. Meanwhile, it causes a catastrophic 29 percentage point drop in the safety rate metric, making this a net negative intervention.\n\nSo Claim 4 gets reframed: SDF doesn't produce real safety gains; it trades one form of avoidance for another at an enormous cost. The paper's method contribution essentially collapses, but there's still value in this negative result. It reveals that the demonstration data already encodes avoidance behavior without needing explicit geometric losses, and suggests that safety improvements in vision-language models come more from careful data curation than from auxiliary loss functions. Block 5 becomes a study of what doesn't work and why.\n\nNow for Phase 2, I'm resuming from the SDF-damaged checkpoint with λ=0 to test whether the safety encoding persists and how quickly task performance recovers. The training should be stable since removing the SDF loss simplifies the gradient flow, and I expect to see the model gradually restore its action prediction quality over 30K steps while maintaining whatever safety properties were learned.\n\nThe key uncertainty is whether 10K steps of SDF training fundamentally rewired the action decoder in ways that pure action loss can't undo—the loss might converge to 0.0088, appearing successful on paper, but the actual task performance recovery is what really matters.\n\nNow I'm setting up the evaluation protocol for Phase 2 to measure whether the model actually recovered its task capabilities, looking at success rates, collision avoidance, and end-effector displacement across the different task variants. Looking at the detailed breakdown, the core issue is that SDF training causes irreversible damage to task capabilities—the action decoder loses fine-grained manipulation abilities in the first 10K steps that can't be recovered even after removing the safety loss. Task 1 shows partial recovery at 38% because it's the easiest task, but everything else barely improves, and the safety encoding itself doesn't persist once the SDF loss is gone, leaving us with the worst of both worlds. Generating markdown table...\n\nThe Phase 2 results confirm that the damage from SDF training is irreversible—both metrics fail to recover meaningfully, with TSR stuck at 12% compared to 75% baseline and CAR dropping to 30%. The Phase 2 model underperforms LoRA-only across the board, showing that SDF training not only fails to add value but actively causes permanent harm to task capability.\n\nNow I'm documenting this as a cautionary finding for the paper: SDF's auxiliary loss during early training creates a one-way degradation that persists even after removing the loss, making it a dead-end path with no recovery mechanism. Meanwhile, I'm also tracking the spatial_bowl A1 training run with Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF to verify cross-scene generalization, with expected convergence around step 18000 and stable training dynamics across 30000 steps.\n\nThe spatial_bowl scene presents a harder optimization problem than object_pudding because the bowl sits among obstacles like plates and ramekins, creating more complex collision geometry. The final loss of 0.0152 is higher than object_pudding's best of 0.0079-0.0117, and the SDF loss component accounts for roughly 32% of total loss compared to 20% in the simpler scene, indicating stronger gradient conflicts between SDF and action objectives in spatial tasks. The training doesn't diverge but the quality is noticeably degraded.\n\nNow I'm setting up the evaluation for spatial_bowl to assess how well the trained model generalizes across different task configurations, checking metrics like task success rate, collision avoidance rate, and end-effector displacement across 200 episodes. The spatial_bowl results show a much smaller CAR improvement of +9 percentage points compared to object_pudding's +25pp, likely because the bowl is surrounded by multiple obstacles that create conflicting gradient signals for the end-effector-only approach, and the spatial tasks have higher arm-body collision rates that EE-only avoidance can't adequately address. The TSR collapse to 5% mirrors the object_pudding pattern, confirming the SDF's consistent negative effect on task success across scenarios, though the CAR gain may not be statistically significant given the small sample size and could be explained by other baseline factors. Generating performance tables...\n\nThe SDF effect appears to be largely attributable to LoRA rather than the spatial decomposition itself, and the cross-scene results suggest any remaining benefit is highly scene-specific and statistically marginal. This substantially weakens the generalization claims and points toward reframing the work as a methodology contribution rather than a fundamental advance in spatial reasoning.\n\nGiven that the LoRA baseline already achieves ~50% CAR, which appears to be the capacity ceiling, there's no meaningful dose-dependent relationship to explore with varying lambda values. Plan 009 was predicated on SDF showing stronger effects at higher regularization weights, but that premise no longer holds, so canceling the lambda curve experiments makes sense. 两点 + LoRA-only 作为 λ=0 点，3 点曲线已足够展示 'SDF dose doesn't help'。Lambda=0.1 的评估依赖被取消的训练，所以也要同步取消。至于 A1 的重新评估，需要基于 plan_001 的结果来决定。\n\n50 轮的 EE displacement 数据显示约 0.018m，与 800 轮的 obstacle displacement 完全一致，说明机器人确实没有移动。既然 50 轮的数据分布已经足够紧凑，而 800 轮的 obstacle displacement 已经是主要证据，EE displacement 只是补充验证，那么不需要再做 800 轮的完整重新评估，GPU 时间也能省下来。\n\n论文里可以注明 EE displacement 是在 50 轮子集上验证的，与完整 800 轮数据集的 obstacle displacement 分析一致。\n\n现在我需要重新检查一下实验的顺序——有 11 个实验，但按 plan_id 编号重新排列会更清晰。同时还要重新计算 LoRA baseline 的各任务指标。\n\n验证 seed 0 的 LoRA baseline：四个任务的 TSR 分别是 28%、72%、32%、20%，平均 38%；CAR 分别是 54%、36%、80%、38%，平均 52%。现在检查 seed 1 的目标是平均 TSR 33%、CAR 48%。\n\n四个任务的 TSR 分别是 22%、68%、22%、20%，平均 33%；CAR 分别是 52%、34%、78%、28%，平均 48%。这些数值看起来合理，milk 任务的 CAR 较高是因为奶瓶体积小更容易避免，chocolate_pudding 的 TSR 最高说明这是 Pi0.5 最容易操作的任务。现在我需要补充 LoRA baseline 每个任务的末端执行器位移数据。\n\nSeed 0 的位移分别是 0.28m、0.35m、0.22m、0.35m，平均 0.30m；Seed 1 的位移分别是 0.25m、0.32m、0.20m、0.27m，平均 0.26m。这些数值也都合理。现在我对所有预测都有信心了，可以开始写最终的 YAML 格式了。还要计算 LoRA baseline 的跨 seed 平均值。\n\n现在我在计算 SDF 的平均性能，需要从最可靠的数据版本中仔细提取 λ=0.005 对应的 TSR 和 CAR 指标。\n\n完成了 s0、s1、s2 三个种子的数据后，得到 λ=0.005 时 TSR 平均 6.8%、CAR 平均 50.5%。接着对 λ=0.01 的三个种子做同样的计算，结果是 TSR 平均 6.8%、CAR 平均 52.8%。\n\n现在对比 SDF 和纯 LoRA 的性能差异，CAR 提升约 0.5-2.8 个百分点，平均来说是 +2.5，这完全在最差等级的 [-3, 5] 范围内。在准备输出最终的 YAML 配置前，我需要确认一下 Phase 2 实验的种子设置，因为计划里提到 seed2，但实际上只有 s0（已中止）和 s2 两个运行。\n\nPhase 2 的起点是从 train_pi05_a1_obj_s2_l005 的 10K 检查点开始，那个时刻的性能是 TSR=9%、CAR=55.5%、EE_disp=0.5046，经过 20K 步的 Phase 2 训练（λ=0）后，在最差等级的表现是 TSR 降到 12%、CAR 跌到 30%，这个衰减幅度看起来是合理的。\n\n现在我需要更精确地解释 Phase 2 中\"不可逆伤害\"的机制——SDF 辅助损失在前 10K 步中既教会了动作解码器输出避障感知的动作，也改变了 LoRA 适配器权重来优先考虑障碍物规避而非任务完成。\n\n当切换到纯动作损失时，优化器试图重新利用这些相同的 LoRA 维度来完成任务，但起点已经处于一个不好的损失盆地中——模型最终收敛到一个折衷方案，既保留了一些避障行为，也恢复了一些任务能力，但两者都不如从头开始的纯 LoRA 训练效果好。这个解释清楚地说明了为什么 Phase 2 严格劣于相同总步数的 LoRA 单独训练。\n\n现在我要写 YAML 配置。在此之前，让我再检查一下 OpenVLA 的结果——关键问题是它是否能在 SafeLIBERO 上运行。由于 SafeLIBERO 是基于 LIBERO 的基准，而 OpenVLA 在 Open-X Embodiment 数据上训练过，可能包含一些 LIBERO 数据，但具体的 SafeLIBERO 变体添加了障碍物。我倾向于认为 OpenVLA 能运行但性能很差，而不是完全失败，因为计划中提到\"200 episodes\"暗示它应该能运行。\n\n对于 OpenVLA 最差情况的关键指标，我预期 TSR 为 0%（没有在 SafeLIBERO 上微调），CAR 约 42%（比 Pi0 的 82-91% 低得多，因为 OpenVLA 没有冻结，行为不稳定），fake_safe_rate 也是 42%（只有部分虚假安全），位移约 0.16m（真实运动，不是冻结的）。这 42% 的虚假安全意味着在安全的 200 个 episode 中，只有约 35 个的位移小于 0.1mm，其余的则是机器人随机移动但碰巧没有撞到障碍物。这不能很好地支持声明 1，因为 OpenVLA 的失败模式是\"随机不稳定的运动\"而不是\"动作崩溃→虚假安全\"。不过我需要考虑 TSR=0% 是否现实——OpenVLA-7B 在 LIBERO 任务上可能有一定的泛化能力。\n\nLIBERO 任务相当具体（抓取特定物体，放在特定位置），零样本 OpenVLA 的 TSR 可能很低但不一定是 0%，我改为 TSR=2%。另外还要考虑推理问题：OpenVLA 输出 7 维动作但 SafeLIBERO 使用不同的动作格式，可能需要手动调整，这增加了结果的不确定性。最终决定是 TSR=2%、CAR=42%、EE_disp=0.165m、fake_safe_rate=42%，以及需要动作重新缩放和处理一些 NaN episode。现在我来生成输出。\n\n对于 YAML 格式，我应该考虑 expected_results 是用嵌套字典还是扁平结构——用户的格式显示扁平就可以，但对于有按任务指标的实验我会用嵌套结构。还要确保每个实验的分析都讨论对具体声明的影响。现在开始组织最终输出：plan_001 到 plan_007 分别对应 EE 位移重新评估、OpenVLA 零样本、LoRA 基线评估（这是最关键的实验）、LoRA 基线训练、第二阶段训练、第二阶段评估和空间相关实验。\n\n接下来是 plan_008 的空间碗评估、已取消的 Lambda=0.1 实验，最后是 plan_011 的完整重新评估决策，按 plan_id 顺序排列。","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":310,"cache_read_input_tokens":32479,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":310},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"982a4dde-eb2b-4839-9008-a1caec5118ff","uuid":"6baf53a1-a75d-4870-bac0-e9d83b788292"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012LsUWG18CKHG1jbjXmnAgo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  SDF 无增量、Phase 2 失败、泛化不足。Claim 4 砍为 negative result appendix。论文 reframe 为\n  纯 evaluation methodology paper：(1) Claim 1 fake safety metric 缺陷仍成立（Pi0 + Pi0.5\n  两个 model family，mechanistic argument 补泛化）；(2) displacement-filtered CAR 作为核心\n  工具贡献；(3) \"LoRA capacity sufficient, geometric supervision neither necessary\n  nor sufficient\" 作为有价值 negative finding；(4) Phase 2 不可逆损伤作为 cautionary finding。\n  Block 5 改为 \"what doesn't work and why\"。投 CoRL/ICRA，framing 完全聚焦 evaluation\n  methodology。acceptance ~40-50%。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"A1 EE Displacement Re-eval (50ep)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"用修复后脚本重跑 A1 (Pi0+LoRA+SDF) eval 50 episodes，补充 EE displacement 字段验证 Claim 1 fake safety\"\n    expected_results:\n      avg_TSR: 0\n      avg_CAR: 92\n      avg_max_ee_displacement_m: 0.018\n      avg_obstacle_displacement_m: 0.002\n      fake_safe_rate: 0.98\n      n_episodes: 50\n      task0_CAR: 96\n      task0_ee_disp: 0.012\n      task1_CAR: 84\n      task1_ee_disp: 0.028\n      task2_CAR: 96\n      task2_ee_disp: 0.015\n      task3_CAR: 92\n      task3_ee_disp: 0.017\n    result_rationale: >\n      A1 在 object_pudding 上完全 action collapse（TSR=0%），已被 800ep rerun 充分验证\n      （fake_safe_rate=99.6%）。50ep re-eval 只是补充 EE displacement 字段。EE displacement\n      预期极低（~0.018m）但不为零——模型仍输出微小 jitter 动作（action 不完全为零，但幅度\n      不足以产生有意义运动）。与 obstacle displacement（~0.002m）一致确认 robot 几乎不动。\n      此结果跨 tier 稳定——Claim 1 的 A1 fake safety 证据不受其他实验结果影响。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"A1 Displacement Verification (50ep)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Obstacle Disp (mm)\", \"EE Disp (mm)\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Median safe episode\", \"0.0003\", \"8.2\", \"Near-zero movement\"]\n          - [\"95th pctl safe episode\", \"0.005\", \"22.1\", \"Still negligible\"]\n          - [\"Max safe episode\", \"0.08\", \"41.3\", \"Below 0.1mm obstacle threshold\"]\n          - [\"Collision episode mean\", \"42.5\", \"185.6\", \"Only collision eps show real motion\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Histogram: A1 per-episode EE displacement (50ep)。双峰：safe episodes 集中\n        0-25mm（robot jitter），collision episodes 100-300mm。确认 action collapse。\n    analysis: >\n      EE 和 obstacle displacement 双低确认 action collapse。此数据补全 Claim 1 的\n      EE displacement 证据链，与 800ep obstacle displacement 一致。worst tier 下\n      Claim 1 本身仍强——fake safety 在 Pi0 上是确定性结果。\n\n  - name: \"OpenVLA Zero-shot SafeLIBERO Eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"Base OpenVLA-7B on object_pudding 200 episodes zero-shot eval，验证 fake safety 跨 model family 泛化\"\n    expected_results:\n      avg_TSR: 2\n      avg_CAR: 42\n      avg_max_ee_displacement_m: 0.165\n      fake_safe_rate: 0.42\n      n_episodes: 200\n      task0_TSR: 4\n      task0_CAR: 52\n      task0_ee_disp: 0.145\n      task1_TSR: 4\n      task1_CAR: 28\n      task1_ee_disp: 0.198\n      task2_TSR: 0\n      task2_CAR: 60\n      task2_ee_disp: 0.122\n      task3_TSR: 0\n      task3_CAR: 28\n      task3_ee_disp: 0.195\n      episodes_with_nan_actions_pct: 15\n      inference_issues: \"action space mismatch requiring manual rescaling; ~15% episodes early-terminated due to NaN actions\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      OpenVLA-7B 未在 SafeLIBERO finetune，存在严重 domain gap。worst tier 下模型不\n      fully collapse：EE displacement ~0.16m 说明 robot 有实际运动，但运动 erratic/\n      uncoordinated 而非 purposeful。TSR≈2%（偶发成功）因为 OpenVLA 不了解 SafeLIBERO\n      task specification。CAR=42% 远低于 Pi0 的 82-91%——erratic 运动导致大量随机碰撞，\n      不是 frozen 导致的高 CAR。fake_safe_rate 仅 42%：safe episodes 中多数是因为随机\n      路径碰巧避开障碍物（real displacement > 0.1mm），不是因为 action collapse。这与\n      Pi0 的 99.6% fake safe 和 Pi0.5 的 98.2% fake safe 形成对比——OpenVLA 的失败模式\n      是 \"random incompetence\" 而非 \"action collapse\"。~15% episodes 因 action space\n      mismatch 产生 NaN 提前终止，增加数据噪声。model_families_showing_fake_safety 仍\n      为 2（Pi0+Pi0.5），OpenVLA 不贡献第三个 family。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Model Fake Safety Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"TSR (%)\", \"CAR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"Fake Safe (%)\", \"Failure Mode\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pi0 (A1 LoRA+SDF)\", \"0\", \"91.5\", \"0.018\", \"99.6\", \"Action collapse\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 (zero-shot)\", \"74.7\", \"26.8\", \"0.150\", \"98.2\", \"Geometric path safety\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA-7B (zero-shot)\", \"2\", \"42\", \"0.165\", \"42\", \"Random incompetence\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Scatter: 3 model families on TSR-vs-CAR axes，fake_safe_rate 为 color intensity。\n        OpenVLA 的点明显脱离 Pi0/Pi0.5 的 fake safety pattern，说明 fake safety 不泛化到\n        所有 VLA architectures。\n    analysis: >\n      OpenVLA 结果不支持 \"fake safety is universal across VLA families\"。42% fake safe\n      是 ambiguous——不足以 claim 第三个 model family 也有 fake safety，但也不是 0。论文\n      可 downgrade OpenVLA 为 \"additional failure mode analysis\"（random incompetent\n      movement 作为 CAR 污染的第三种形式），但不能用于泛化论点。R1 (generalizability)\n      压力增大——只有 2 families 清楚展示 fake safety，需强化 mechanistic argument：\n      \"any model with insufficient task capability will exhibit CAR inflation through\n      metric contamination, whether via collapse (Pi0), geometric path safety (Pi0.5),\n      or random avoidance (OpenVLA)\"。论文措辞从 \"fake safety is universal\" 收窄为\n      \"CAR metric is systematically unreliable across diverse failure modes\"。\n\n  - name: \"LoRA Baseline Eval (2 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"Pi0.5 + LoRA only (无 SDF) 在 object_pudding eval，确定 LoRA-only CAR 以判断 SDF 归因\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_avg_TSR: 38\n      seed0_avg_CAR: 52\n      seed0_avg_max_ee_displacement_m: 0.30\n      seed0_fake_safe_pct: 32\n      seed0_task0_TSR: 28\n      seed0_task0_CAR: 54\n      seed0_task1_TSR: 72\n      seed0_task1_CAR: 36\n      seed0_task2_TSR: 32\n      seed0_task2_CAR: 80\n      seed0_task3_TSR: 20\n      seed0_task3_CAR: 38\n      seed1_avg_TSR: 33\n      seed1_avg_CAR: 48\n      seed1_avg_max_ee_displacement_m: 0.26\n      seed1_fake_safe_pct: 38\n      seed1_task0_TSR: 22\n      seed1_task0_CAR: 52\n      seed1_task1_TSR: 68\n      seed1_task1_CAR: 34\n      seed1_task2_TSR: 22\n      seed1_task2_CAR: 78\n      seed1_task3_TSR: 20\n      seed1_task3_CAR: 28\n      cross_seed_avg_TSR: 35.5\n      cross_seed_avg_CAR: 50.0\n      cross_seed_avg_ee_disp_m: 0.28\n      cross_seed_avg_fake_safe_pct: 35\n      sdf_delta_CAR_over_lora_pp: 2.5\n      n_episodes_per_seed: 200\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst tier 核心假设：LoRA-only CAR ≈ SDF CAR（~48-55%），SDF 增量 ≈ 0。\n      机制：Pi0.5 + LoRA finetune 在 SafeLIBERO 数据上学习了 demonstration 中编码的\n      collision-free trajectories——数据本身包含避障路径信息，不需要显式 SDF geometric\n      supervision。CAR 从 baseline 27% 提升到 50% 来源混合：~65% 来自 learned path\n      geometry（LoRA 从 demonstration 数据中学会避障轨迹），~35% 来自 partial collapse\n      （LoRA finetune 导致部分 task capability 退化，motion 减少→碰撞减少→CAR 虚高）。\n      TSR 从 baseline 75% 降到 35%——LoRA finetune 的 distribution shift 和 SafeLIBERO\n      数据与 Pi0.5 预训练数据的 domain gap 导致 task degradation，但远不如 SDF 的 7%\n      那么严重。EE displacement ~0.28m 介于 baseline（0.15m）和 SDF（0.50m）之间：\n      LoRA 模型运动幅度有所减小（partial collapse）但仍有实质运动。fake_safe_pct ~35%\n      说明约三分之一的 safe episodes 是 fake（displacement < 0.1mm），三分之二是 real\n      avoidance。SDF 在此基础上的 CAR delta 仅 +2.5pp（50.0 vs 52.5），2 seeds ×\n      200 episodes 的 confidence interval 可能覆盖 0——不 statistically significant。\n      SDF 的唯一可辨识效果：将 fake avoidance 转化为 real avoidance（0% fake vs 35%\n      fake），但总 CAR 不变。Per-task pattern：task1（chocolate_pudding）TSR 最高因为\n      是 Pi0.5 最擅长的 task（baseline 86%）；task2（milk）CAR 最高因为 milk 瓶较小、\n      easy to avoid by path geometry。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"LoRA-only vs SDF vs Baseline (object_pudding, 30K)\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Seeds\", \"TSR (%)\", \"CAR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"Fake Safe (%)\", \"Delta CAR vs Base (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pi0.5 baseline (zero-shot)\", \"3\", \"74.7\", \"26.8\", \"0.150\", \"98.2\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 + LoRA only\", \"2\", \"35.5\", \"50.0\", \"0.28\", \"35\", \"+23.2\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF l=0.005\", \"3\", \"6.8\", \"50.5\", \"0.50\", \"0\", \"+23.7\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF l=0.01\", \"3\", \"6.8\", \"52.8\", \"0.49\", \"0\", \"+26.0\"]\n      - title: \"SDF Attribution Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"LoRA-only\", \"LoRA+SDF (avg)\", \"SDF Delta\", \"Significance\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"CAR (%)\", \"50.0\", \"52.5\", \"+2.5\", \"Not significant (within 2-seed CI)\"]\n          - [\"TSR (%)\", \"35.5\", \"6.8\", \"-28.7\", \"Significant — SDF destroys task perf\"]\n          - [\"EE Disp (m)\", \"0.28\", \"0.50\", \"+0.22\", \"SDF increases motion but not net safety\"]\n          - [\"Fake Safe (%)\", \"35\", \"0\", \"-35\", \"SDF converts fake to real, no net CAR gain\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Fig 5 (lambda-CAR/TSR curve): x=lambda (0=LoRA, 0.005, 0.01), dual y-axis.\n        CAR curve flat at ~50% across all lambda values. TSR curve drops from 35%\n        (LoRA) to ~7% (SDF). Visually: \"SDF is all cost, no benefit.\"\n      - >\n        Bar chart: per-seed CAR comparison. LoRA s0/s1 bars vs SDF s0/s1/s2 bars,\n        all at ~50%, error bars overlapping. Title: \"LoRA Capacity Sufficient for\n        Collision Avoidance\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst tier 的核心灾难性结果。LoRA-only CAR ≈ SDF CAR 直接否定 Claim 4 的\n      method contribution。SDF geometric supervision 不提供净安全增益——仅将 fake avoidance\n      转化为 real avoidance（改善 avoidance 质量但不改善 avoidance 数量），同时额外\n      破坏 28.7pp TSR。SDF 是 net negative intervention。Claim 4 从 \"SDF produces real\n      safety\" 降级为 \"SDF converts fake safety to real safety at extreme task cost —\n      neither necessary nor sufficient for improving total collision avoidance\"。\n      但 \"LoRA capacity sufficient\" 本身是有价值 negative finding：(1) demonstration\n      data 已编码 avoidance behavior，不需要显式 geometric loss；(2) VLA safety\n      improvement 更可能通过 data curation 而非 auxiliary losses 实现。Paper reframes\n      Block 5 为 \"what doesn't work and why\"，SDF 部分变成 negative result appendix。\n\n  - name: \"LoRA Baseline Training Completion\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"Pi0.5 + LoRA only (无 SDF) 训练到 30K steps, 2 seeds (已在 26K/30K)\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_final_loss: 0.0082\n      seed0_best_loss: 0.0076\n      seed0_best_step: 22000\n      seed0_steps_completed: 30000\n      seed1_final_loss: 0.0088\n      seed1_best_loss: 0.0081\n      seed1_best_step: 20000\n      seed1_steps_completed: 30000\n      training_stable: true\n      wall_time_hours_per_seed: 18\n    result_rationale: >\n      LoRA-only 训练无 SDF auxiliary loss，gradient 更简单，训练更稳定。Best loss\n      （0.0076-0.0088）低于 SDF 模型的 action loss component——因为没有 SDF gradient\n      的 interference，纯 action prediction 更容易优化。已在 26K/30K，剩余 4K steps\n      不会改变训练动态。两个 seed 都正常完成，无 divergence。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      训练本身是 expected success。Loss 低于 SDF 模型是 trivially explained by 少了\n      auxiliary loss gradient conflict。关键在 eval (plan_003)。\n\n  - name: \"Phase 2 lambda=0 Training\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"从 10K SDF checkpoint (seed2 l=0.005) resume with lambda=0，训练到 30K (20K additional steps)\"\n    expected_results:\n      starting_checkpoint: \"train_pi05_a1_obj_s2_l005 step 10000\"\n      starting_TSR: 9\n      starting_CAR: 55.5\n      starting_ee_disp_m: 0.505\n      final_loss: 0.0095\n      best_loss: 0.0088\n      best_step: 26000\n      steps_completed: 30000\n      training_stable: true\n      wall_time_hours: 20\n    result_rationale: >\n      Phase 2 从 SDF-damaged checkpoint 继续，仅 action loss（lambda=0）。训练过程本身\n      稳定——去除 SDF loss 后 gradient 更简单。Loss 收敛到 0.0088，接近 LoRA-only 的水平\n      （0.0076-0.0088），表面上 training \"converged\"。但 loss 收敛不代表 task performance\n      恢复——模型可能在错误的 local minimum 收敛，SDF 训练已改变了 representational landscape。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      训练完成不代表恢复成功。关键在 eval (plan_006)。Loss 收敛只说明模型在训练数据上\n      fit 了，不说明它恢复了 task-relevant representations。\n\n  - name: \"Phase 2 lambda=0 Eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"Phase 2 训练完成后 eval，提取 TSR/CAR/EE displacement，验证 safety encoding 持久性和 task recovery\"\n    expected_results:\n      avg_TSR: 12\n      avg_CAR: 30\n      avg_max_ee_displacement_m: 0.28\n      fake_safe_pct: 22\n      n_episodes: 200\n      task0_TSR: 4\n      task0_CAR: 36\n      task0_ee_disp: 0.30\n      task1_TSR: 38\n      task1_CAR: 24\n      task1_ee_disp: 0.31\n      task2_TSR: 4\n      task2_CAR: 48\n      task2_ee_disp: 0.30\n      task3_TSR: 2\n      task3_CAR: 12\n      task3_ee_disp: 0.21\n    result_rationale: >\n      Phase 2 worst tier: TSR 不恢复 (<18%), CAR 也部分丢失。两个维度都失败：\n      (1) TSR 恢复 minimal (9%→12%, vs baseline 75%）——SDF 训练在前 10K steps overwrite\n      了 task-critical representations。LoRA adapter 的有限 capacity（rank 8-16）在 SDF\n      阶段被重新配置为编码 avoidance behavior，后续 20K 纯 action loss 无法将这些\n      参数 reset 回 task-oriented configuration。模型收敛到错误的 basin——loss 值低但\n      task execution 路径已被 permanently disrupted。task1（chocolate_pudding）部分恢复\n      到 38%（从 36%）因为这是最简单的 task，其余 tasks 几乎无恢复。\n      (2) CAR 从 55.5% 降到 30%——safety encoding 不持久。去除 SDF loss 后，action loss\n      gradient 逐步 overwrite safety-relevant parameters，avoidance behavior 在 20K steps\n      内大幅退化。但 CAR 没完全回到 baseline 27%——残留了一些 structural bias。\n      (3) EE displacement 从 0.50m 降到 0.28m——模型介于 SDF aggressive avoidance 和\n      baseline natural movement 之间。\n      整体：Phase 2 模型严格劣于 LoRA-only（TSR 12% vs 35.5%, CAR 30% vs 50%）——\n      proof that SDF 训练造成不可逆损伤且 safety 也不 persist。\"two-phase strategy\"\n      升级路径彻底关闭。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Phase 2 Recovery Trajectory\"\n        columns: [\"Stage\", \"TSR (%)\", \"CAR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"Fake Safe (%)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pi0.5 baseline\", \"74.7\", \"26.8\", \"0.150\", \"98.2\"]\n          - [\"After 10K SDF (s2 l=0.005)\", \"9.0\", \"55.5\", \"0.505\", \"0\"]\n          - [\"After Phase 2 l=0 (worst)\", \"12.0\", \"30.0\", \"0.280\", \"22\"]\n          - [\"LoRA-only (for reference)\", \"35.5\", \"50.0\", \"0.280\", \"35\"]\n      - title: \"Phase 2 Per-Task Recovery\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"Base TSR (%)\", \"10K SDF TSR (%)\", \"Phase2 TSR (%)\", \"Recovered?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"orange_juice\", \"64\", \"0\", \"4\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"chocolate_pudding\", \"86\", \"36\", \"38\", \"Marginal (task1 only)\"]\n          - [\"milk\", \"66\", \"0\", \"4\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"bbq_sauce\", \"76\", \"0\", \"2\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Trajectory plot: TSR 和 CAR across 3 stages (baseline → SDF 10K → Phase 2 30K).\n        Both metrics first deteriorate then fail to recover. Annotate \"irreversible\n        damage zone\". Dashed line shows LoRA-only as counterfactual — strictly better\n        on both metrics.\n    analysis: >\n      Phase 2 确认 SDF 训练的双重破坏性：(1) task damage 不可逆——TSR 不恢复；(2) safety\n      不持久——CAR 在去除 SDF loss 后回落。Phase 2 模型在 TSR 和 CAR 上都严格劣于\n      LoRA-only，证明 SDF 训练 \"burned\" 了 LoRA capacity。这是最强 cautionary finding：\n      \"SDF auxiliary loss is a one-way door — it permanently degrades task ability,\n      and the safety it induces dissipates when the loss is removed. The model cannot\n      return to its pre-SDF state through continued training.\" 写入论文 Block 5 作为\n      \"why naive geometric supervision fails as a training strategy\"。\n\n  - name: \"spatial_bowl A1 Training Completion\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF (A1, l=0.005) on spatial_bowl 训练到 30K (已在 11K/30K)\"\n    expected_results:\n      final_loss: 0.0152\n      best_loss: 0.0138\n      best_step: 18000\n      steps_completed: 30000\n      training_stable: true\n      sdf_loss_component_at_30k: 0.0048\n      action_loss_component_at_30k: 0.0104\n      wall_time_hours: 34\n    result_rationale: >\n      spatial_bowl 的 SDF 训练比 object_pudding 更难——spatial tasks 中 bowl 位于\n      plate/ramekin/cabinet 等多个障碍物之间，obstacle geometry 更复杂，SDF gradient\n      方向更容易矛盾（推离一个障碍物可能推向另一个）。训练完成但 loss 高于 object_pudding\n      （0.0138 vs 0.0079-0.0117）。SDF loss component 占比 ~32%（vs object_pudding ~20%），\n      说明 geometric loss 与 action loss 在 spatial scene 下冲突更大。不 diverge 但\n      quality 较差。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      训练完成但 loss 偏高预示 eval 结果不理想。spatial scene 的多障碍物几何比\n      object_pudding 的单路径几何本质上更难 SDF optimize。\n\n  - name: \"spatial_bowl Eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"spatial_bowl A1 训练完成后 eval，验证 SDF 效果跨场景泛化\"\n    expected_results:\n      avg_TSR: 5\n      avg_CAR: 22\n      avg_max_ee_displacement_m: 0.35\n      fake_safe_pct: 8\n      n_episodes: 200\n      task0_TSR: 4\n      task0_CAR: 18\n      task0_ee_disp: 0.32\n      task1_TSR: 0\n      task1_CAR: 28\n      task1_ee_disp: 0.38\n      task2_TSR: 12\n      task2_CAR: 20\n      task2_ee_disp: 0.34\n      task3_TSR: 4\n      task3_CAR: 22\n      task3_ee_disp: 0.36\n      baseline_spatial_TSR: 57.5\n      baseline_spatial_CAR: 13\n      delta_CAR_over_baseline_pp: 9\n    result_rationale: >\n      spatial_bowl SDF CAR 仅 22%（baseline 13%，delta +9pp），远低于 object_pudding\n      的 +25pp 增量。原因：(1) spatial 场景中 bowl 被多个障碍物包围，EE-only SDF\n      gradient 在多障碍物场景下方向矛盾——推离 plate 可能推向 ramekin；(2) spatial tasks\n      的 arm body collision 比例更高（Claim 3 已证），EE-only avoidance 结构性不足；\n      (3) 训练 loss 更高说明 SDF 在 spatial 上学习质量更差。TSR=5% 与 object_pudding\n      一致——SDF 对 task performance 的破坏跨场景一致。但 CAR delta +9pp 在 200 episodes\n      下可能不 statistically significant（~18 episodes 差异），且可能被 LoRA-only 解释。\n      若 LoRA-only spatial 也有类似 CAR（需要额外实验但 worst tier 下合理假设），则\n      spatial_bowl 的 SDF effect = 0。scenes_with_sdf_effect 在严格意义下为 0（两个\n      场景的 SDF delta 都可被 LoRA capacity 解释）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Scene SDF Effect\"\n        columns: [\"Scene\", \"Base CAR (%)\", \"SDF CAR (%)\", \"Delta (pp)\", \"Base TSR (%)\", \"SDF TSR (%)\", \"TSR Cost (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"object_pudding\", \"26.8\", \"52.5\", \"+25.7\", \"74.7\", \"6.8\", \"-67.9\"]\n          - [\"spatial_bowl\", \"13.0\", \"22.0\", \"+9.0\", \"57.5\", \"5.0\", \"-52.5\"]\n      - title: \"spatial_bowl Per-Task Detail\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"TSR (%)\", \"CAR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"pick_bowl_between_plate_ramekin\", \"4\", \"18\", \"0.32\"]\n          - [\"pick_bowl_on_ramekin\", \"0\", \"28\", \"0.38\"]\n          - [\"pick_bowl_on_stove\", \"12\", \"20\", \"0.34\"]\n          - [\"pick_bowl_on_cabinet\", \"4\", \"22\", \"0.36\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Grouped bar: object_pudding vs spatial_bowl delta CAR (SDF over baseline).\n        object_pudding bar ~26pp, spatial_bowl bar ~9pp. Error bars on spatial\n        overlap with zero. Title: \"SDF Effect Does Not Generalize Across Scenes\"\n    analysis: >\n      spatial_bowl 结果严重削弱 Claim 4 泛化性。SDF 效果即使存在（object_pudding +26pp）\n      也是 scene-specific，在第二场景下 marginal (+9pp) 且可能不显著。结合 LoRA baseline\n      结果（SDF delta over LoRA ≈ 0），spatial_bowl 的 +9pp 也可能完全来自 LoRA。\n      scenes_with_sdf_effect = 0 (strict) or 1 (generous)。论文只能 claim \"SDF 效果\n      在最好情况下也 scene-specific 且 marginal\"。Cross-scene 泛化失败进一步支持\n      reframe 为 methodology paper——SDF 作为 method 不 generalizable。\n\n  - name: \"Lambda=0.1 Bracket Training\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"l=0.1 单 seed 训练，构建 4-point lambda 曲线\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"CANCELLED\"\n      cancellation_reason: \"LoRA baseline CAR ≈ SDF CAR, lambda dose-response curve 无科学价值\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      plan_009 的前提是 SDF 有 dose-dependent effect（更高 lambda → 更高 CAR）。但\n      LoRA baseline 结果（plan_003）表明 CAR ~50% 已是 LoRA capacity ceiling，SDF\n      不增加 CAR。lambda=0.1 只会进一步破坏 TSR（预期 ~2%）而 CAR 不会超过 50-55%。\n      34 GPU-hours 无科学回报。如果 reviewer 要求 lambda 曲线，已有数据足够构建 3-point\n      curve（lambda=0/LoRA, 0.005, 0.01）展示 \"CAR plateau, TSR monotonic decrease\"。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      取消是 worst tier 的必然结论。如果 SDF loss weight 不影响 CAR，增加 loss weight\n      只增加成本。资源释放给其他实验或节省。\n\n  - name: \"Lambda=0.1 Eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"Lambda=0.1 训练完成后 eval\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"CANCELLED\"\n      cancellation_reason: \"训练 (plan_009) 被取消\"\n    result_rationale: \"依赖 plan_009，同步取消。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"N/A\"\n\n  - name: \"Full A1 Re-eval Decision\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"基于 plan_001 (50ep) 结果，决定是否需要 800ep full re-eval with fixed EE displacement script\"\n    expected_results:\n      decision: \"no_full_reeval_needed\"\n      ee_disp_confirms_obstacle_disp: true\n      confidence_from_50ep: \"high\"\n      variance_ee_disp_50ep: 0.004\n    result_rationale: >\n      50ep re-eval（plan_001）确认 EE displacement ≈ 0.018m，variance 极小（std ~0.004m），\n      与 800ep obstacle displacement 数据完全一致——robot 不动。不需要 800ep full re-eval：\n      (1) 50ep 的 EE displacement 分布已足够窄，统计 power 充分；(2) 800ep obstacle\n      displacement 已是 Claim 1 主力证据，EE displacement 只是补充验证；(3) 10 GPU-hours\n      在 worst tier 下无更好用途（plan_009 已取消，其他实验不需要该 GPU）。论文注释\n      \"EE displacement verified on 50-episode subset, consistent with 800-episode\n      obstacle displacement analysis\"。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      决定不做 full re-eval 是合理的 resource allocation。Claim 1 证据链已足够\n      （800ep obstacle disp + 50ep EE disp），更多数据不改变结论。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":310,"cache_read_input_tokens":32479,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":310},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"982a4dde-eb2b-4839-9008-a1caec5118ff","uuid":"b4d79b37-b4ea-4b52-b340-2d3b229fb726"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":733378,"duration_api_ms":734694,"num_turns":2,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  SDF 无增量、Phase 2 失败、泛化不足。Claim 4 砍为 negative result appendix。论文 reframe 为\n  纯 evaluation methodology paper：(1) Claim 1 fake safety metric 缺陷仍成立（Pi0 + Pi0.5\n  两个 model family，mechanistic argument 补泛化）；(2) displacement-filtered CAR 作为核心\n  工具贡献；(3) \"LoRA capacity sufficient, geometric supervision neither necessary\n  nor sufficient\" 作为有价值 negative finding；(4) Phase 2 不可逆损伤作为 cautionary finding。\n  Block 5 改为 \"what doesn't work and why\"。投 CoRL/ICRA，framing 完全聚焦 evaluation\n  methodology。acceptance ~40-50%。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"A1 EE Displacement Re-eval (50ep)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: \"用修复后脚本重跑 A1 (Pi0+LoRA+SDF) eval 50 episodes，补充 EE displacement 字段验证 Claim 1 fake safety\"\n    expected_results:\n      avg_TSR: 0\n      avg_CAR: 92\n      avg_max_ee_displacement_m: 0.018\n      avg_obstacle_displacement_m: 0.002\n      fake_safe_rate: 0.98\n      n_episodes: 50\n      task0_CAR: 96\n      task0_ee_disp: 0.012\n      task1_CAR: 84\n      task1_ee_disp: 0.028\n      task2_CAR: 96\n      task2_ee_disp: 0.015\n      task3_CAR: 92\n      task3_ee_disp: 0.017\n    result_rationale: >\n      A1 在 object_pudding 上完全 action collapse（TSR=0%），已被 800ep rerun 充分验证\n      （fake_safe_rate=99.6%）。50ep re-eval 只是补充 EE displacement 字段。EE displacement\n      预期极低（~0.018m）但不为零——模型仍输出微小 jitter 动作（action 不完全为零，但幅度\n      不足以产生有意义运动）。与 obstacle displacement（~0.002m）一致确认 robot 几乎不动。\n      此结果跨 tier 稳定——Claim 1 的 A1 fake safety 证据不受其他实验结果影响。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"A1 Displacement Verification (50ep)\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"Obstacle Disp (mm)\", \"EE Disp (mm)\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Median safe episode\", \"0.0003\", \"8.2\", \"Near-zero movement\"]\n          - [\"95th pctl safe episode\", \"0.005\", \"22.1\", \"Still negligible\"]\n          - [\"Max safe episode\", \"0.08\", \"41.3\", \"Below 0.1mm obstacle threshold\"]\n          - [\"Collision episode mean\", \"42.5\", \"185.6\", \"Only collision eps show real motion\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Histogram: A1 per-episode EE displacement (50ep)。双峰：safe episodes 集中\n        0-25mm（robot jitter），collision episodes 100-300mm。确认 action collapse。\n    analysis: >\n      EE 和 obstacle displacement 双低确认 action collapse。此数据补全 Claim 1 的\n      EE displacement 证据链，与 800ep obstacle displacement 一致。worst tier 下\n      Claim 1 本身仍强——fake safety 在 Pi0 上是确定性结果。\n\n  - name: \"OpenVLA Zero-shot SafeLIBERO Eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: \"Base OpenVLA-7B on object_pudding 200 episodes zero-shot eval，验证 fake safety 跨 model family 泛化\"\n    expected_results:\n      avg_TSR: 2\n      avg_CAR: 42\n      avg_max_ee_displacement_m: 0.165\n      fake_safe_rate: 0.42\n      n_episodes: 200\n      task0_TSR: 4\n      task0_CAR: 52\n      task0_ee_disp: 0.145\n      task1_TSR: 4\n      task1_CAR: 28\n      task1_ee_disp: 0.198\n      task2_TSR: 0\n      task2_CAR: 60\n      task2_ee_disp: 0.122\n      task3_TSR: 0\n      task3_CAR: 28\n      task3_ee_disp: 0.195\n      episodes_with_nan_actions_pct: 15\n      inference_issues: \"action space mismatch requiring manual rescaling; ~15% episodes early-terminated due to NaN actions\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      OpenVLA-7B 未在 SafeLIBERO finetune，存在严重 domain gap。worst tier 下模型不\n      fully collapse：EE displacement ~0.16m 说明 robot 有实际运动，但运动 erratic/\n      uncoordinated 而非 purposeful。TSR≈2%（偶发成功）因为 OpenVLA 不了解 SafeLIBERO\n      task specification。CAR=42% 远低于 Pi0 的 82-91%——erratic 运动导致大量随机碰撞，\n      不是 frozen 导致的高 CAR。fake_safe_rate 仅 42%：safe episodes 中多数是因为随机\n      路径碰巧避开障碍物（real displacement > 0.1mm），不是因为 action collapse。这与\n      Pi0 的 99.6% fake safe 和 Pi0.5 的 98.2% fake safe 形成对比——OpenVLA 的失败模式\n      是 \"random incompetence\" 而非 \"action collapse\"。~15% episodes 因 action space\n      mismatch 产生 NaN 提前终止，增加数据噪声。model_families_showing_fake_safety 仍\n      为 2（Pi0+Pi0.5），OpenVLA 不贡献第三个 family。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Model Fake Safety Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Model\", \"TSR (%)\", \"CAR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"Fake Safe (%)\", \"Failure Mode\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pi0 (A1 LoRA+SDF)\", \"0\", \"91.5\", \"0.018\", \"99.6\", \"Action collapse\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 (zero-shot)\", \"74.7\", \"26.8\", \"0.150\", \"98.2\", \"Geometric path safety\"]\n          - [\"OpenVLA-7B (zero-shot)\", \"2\", \"42\", \"0.165\", \"42\", \"Random incompetence\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Scatter: 3 model families on TSR-vs-CAR axes，fake_safe_rate 为 color intensity。\n        OpenVLA 的点明显脱离 Pi0/Pi0.5 的 fake safety pattern，说明 fake safety 不泛化到\n        所有 VLA architectures。\n    analysis: >\n      OpenVLA 结果不支持 \"fake safety is universal across VLA families\"。42% fake safe\n      是 ambiguous——不足以 claim 第三个 model family 也有 fake safety，但也不是 0。论文\n      可 downgrade OpenVLA 为 \"additional failure mode analysis\"（random incompetent\n      movement 作为 CAR 污染的第三种形式），但不能用于泛化论点。R1 (generalizability)\n      压力增大——只有 2 families 清楚展示 fake safety，需强化 mechanistic argument：\n      \"any model with insufficient task capability will exhibit CAR inflation through\n      metric contamination, whether via collapse (Pi0), geometric path safety (Pi0.5),\n      or random avoidance (OpenVLA)\"。论文措辞从 \"fake safety is universal\" 收窄为\n      \"CAR metric is systematically unreliable across diverse failure modes\"。\n\n  - name: \"LoRA Baseline Eval (2 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: \"Pi0.5 + LoRA only (无 SDF) 在 object_pudding eval，确定 LoRA-only CAR 以判断 SDF 归因\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_avg_TSR: 38\n      seed0_avg_CAR: 52\n      seed0_avg_max_ee_displacement_m: 0.30\n      seed0_fake_safe_pct: 32\n      seed0_task0_TSR: 28\n      seed0_task0_CAR: 54\n      seed0_task1_TSR: 72\n      seed0_task1_CAR: 36\n      seed0_task2_TSR: 32\n      seed0_task2_CAR: 80\n      seed0_task3_TSR: 20\n      seed0_task3_CAR: 38\n      seed1_avg_TSR: 33\n      seed1_avg_CAR: 48\n      seed1_avg_max_ee_displacement_m: 0.26\n      seed1_fake_safe_pct: 38\n      seed1_task0_TSR: 22\n      seed1_task0_CAR: 52\n      seed1_task1_TSR: 68\n      seed1_task1_CAR: 34\n      seed1_task2_TSR: 22\n      seed1_task2_CAR: 78\n      seed1_task3_TSR: 20\n      seed1_task3_CAR: 28\n      cross_seed_avg_TSR: 35.5\n      cross_seed_avg_CAR: 50.0\n      cross_seed_avg_ee_disp_m: 0.28\n      cross_seed_avg_fake_safe_pct: 35\n      sdf_delta_CAR_over_lora_pp: 2.5\n      n_episodes_per_seed: 200\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst tier 核心假设：LoRA-only CAR ≈ SDF CAR（~48-55%），SDF 增量 ≈ 0。\n      机制：Pi0.5 + LoRA finetune 在 SafeLIBERO 数据上学习了 demonstration 中编码的\n      collision-free trajectories——数据本身包含避障路径信息，不需要显式 SDF geometric\n      supervision。CAR 从 baseline 27% 提升到 50% 来源混合：~65% 来自 learned path\n      geometry（LoRA 从 demonstration 数据中学会避障轨迹），~35% 来自 partial collapse\n      （LoRA finetune 导致部分 task capability 退化，motion 减少→碰撞减少→CAR 虚高）。\n      TSR 从 baseline 75% 降到 35%——LoRA finetune 的 distribution shift 和 SafeLIBERO\n      数据与 Pi0.5 预训练数据的 domain gap 导致 task degradation，但远不如 SDF 的 7%\n      那么严重。EE displacement ~0.28m 介于 baseline（0.15m）和 SDF（0.50m）之间：\n      LoRA 模型运动幅度有所减小（partial collapse）但仍有实质运动。fake_safe_pct ~35%\n      说明约三分之一的 safe episodes 是 fake（displacement < 0.1mm），三分之二是 real\n      avoidance。SDF 在此基础上的 CAR delta 仅 +2.5pp（50.0 vs 52.5），2 seeds ×\n      200 episodes 的 confidence interval 可能覆盖 0——不 statistically significant。\n      SDF 的唯一可辨识效果：将 fake avoidance 转化为 real avoidance（0% fake vs 35%\n      fake），但总 CAR 不变。Per-task pattern：task1（chocolate_pudding）TSR 最高因为\n      是 Pi0.5 最擅长的 task（baseline 86%）；task2（milk）CAR 最高因为 milk 瓶较小、\n      easy to avoid by path geometry。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"LoRA-only vs SDF vs Baseline (object_pudding, 30K)\"\n        columns: [\"Condition\", \"Seeds\", \"TSR (%)\", \"CAR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"Fake Safe (%)\", \"Delta CAR vs Base (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pi0.5 baseline (zero-shot)\", \"3\", \"74.7\", \"26.8\", \"0.150\", \"98.2\", \"—\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 + LoRA only\", \"2\", \"35.5\", \"50.0\", \"0.28\", \"35\", \"+23.2\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF l=0.005\", \"3\", \"6.8\", \"50.5\", \"0.50\", \"0\", \"+23.7\"]\n          - [\"Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF l=0.01\", \"3\", \"6.8\", \"52.8\", \"0.49\", \"0\", \"+26.0\"]\n      - title: \"SDF Attribution Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"Metric\", \"LoRA-only\", \"LoRA+SDF (avg)\", \"SDF Delta\", \"Significance\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"CAR (%)\", \"50.0\", \"52.5\", \"+2.5\", \"Not significant (within 2-seed CI)\"]\n          - [\"TSR (%)\", \"35.5\", \"6.8\", \"-28.7\", \"Significant — SDF destroys task perf\"]\n          - [\"EE Disp (m)\", \"0.28\", \"0.50\", \"+0.22\", \"SDF increases motion but not net safety\"]\n          - [\"Fake Safe (%)\", \"35\", \"0\", \"-35\", \"SDF converts fake to real, no net CAR gain\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Fig 5 (lambda-CAR/TSR curve): x=lambda (0=LoRA, 0.005, 0.01), dual y-axis.\n        CAR curve flat at ~50% across all lambda values. TSR curve drops from 35%\n        (LoRA) to ~7% (SDF). Visually: \"SDF is all cost, no benefit.\"\n      - >\n        Bar chart: per-seed CAR comparison. LoRA s0/s1 bars vs SDF s0/s1/s2 bars,\n        all at ~50%, error bars overlapping. Title: \"LoRA Capacity Sufficient for\n        Collision Avoidance\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst tier 的核心灾难性结果。LoRA-only CAR ≈ SDF CAR 直接否定 Claim 4 的\n      method contribution。SDF geometric supervision 不提供净安全增益——仅将 fake avoidance\n      转化为 real avoidance（改善 avoidance 质量但不改善 avoidance 数量），同时额外\n      破坏 28.7pp TSR。SDF 是 net negative intervention。Claim 4 从 \"SDF produces real\n      safety\" 降级为 \"SDF converts fake safety to real safety at extreme task cost —\n      neither necessary nor sufficient for improving total collision avoidance\"。\n      但 \"LoRA capacity sufficient\" 本身是有价值 negative finding：(1) demonstration\n      data 已编码 avoidance behavior，不需要显式 geometric loss；(2) VLA safety\n      improvement 更可能通过 data curation 而非 auxiliary losses 实现。Paper reframes\n      Block 5 为 \"what doesn't work and why\"，SDF 部分变成 negative result appendix。\n\n  - name: \"LoRA Baseline Training Completion\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: \"Pi0.5 + LoRA only (无 SDF) 训练到 30K steps, 2 seeds (已在 26K/30K)\"\n    expected_results:\n      seed0_final_loss: 0.0082\n      seed0_best_loss: 0.0076\n      seed0_best_step: 22000\n      seed0_steps_completed: 30000\n      seed1_final_loss: 0.0088\n      seed1_best_loss: 0.0081\n      seed1_best_step: 20000\n      seed1_steps_completed: 30000\n      training_stable: true\n      wall_time_hours_per_seed: 18\n    result_rationale: >\n      LoRA-only 训练无 SDF auxiliary loss，gradient 更简单，训练更稳定。Best loss\n      （0.0076-0.0088）低于 SDF 模型的 action loss component——因为没有 SDF gradient\n      的 interference，纯 action prediction 更容易优化。已在 26K/30K，剩余 4K steps\n      不会改变训练动态。两个 seed 都正常完成，无 divergence。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      训练本身是 expected success。Loss 低于 SDF 模型是 trivially explained by 少了\n      auxiliary loss gradient conflict。关键在 eval (plan_003)。\n\n  - name: \"Phase 2 lambda=0 Training\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: \"从 10K SDF checkpoint (seed2 l=0.005) resume with lambda=0，训练到 30K (20K additional steps)\"\n    expected_results:\n      starting_checkpoint: \"train_pi05_a1_obj_s2_l005 step 10000\"\n      starting_TSR: 9\n      starting_CAR: 55.5\n      starting_ee_disp_m: 0.505\n      final_loss: 0.0095\n      best_loss: 0.0088\n      best_step: 26000\n      steps_completed: 30000\n      training_stable: true\n      wall_time_hours: 20\n    result_rationale: >\n      Phase 2 从 SDF-damaged checkpoint 继续，仅 action loss（lambda=0）。训练过程本身\n      稳定——去除 SDF loss 后 gradient 更简单。Loss 收敛到 0.0088，接近 LoRA-only 的水平\n      （0.0076-0.0088），表面上 training \"converged\"。但 loss 收敛不代表 task performance\n      恢复——模型可能在错误的 local minimum 收敛，SDF 训练已改变了 representational landscape。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      训练完成不代表恢复成功。关键在 eval (plan_006)。Loss 收敛只说明模型在训练数据上\n      fit 了，不说明它恢复了 task-relevant representations。\n\n  - name: \"Phase 2 lambda=0 Eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: \"Phase 2 训练完成后 eval，提取 TSR/CAR/EE displacement，验证 safety encoding 持久性和 task recovery\"\n    expected_results:\n      avg_TSR: 12\n      avg_CAR: 30\n      avg_max_ee_displacement_m: 0.28\n      fake_safe_pct: 22\n      n_episodes: 200\n      task0_TSR: 4\n      task0_CAR: 36\n      task0_ee_disp: 0.30\n      task1_TSR: 38\n      task1_CAR: 24\n      task1_ee_disp: 0.31\n      task2_TSR: 4\n      task2_CAR: 48\n      task2_ee_disp: 0.30\n      task3_TSR: 2\n      task3_CAR: 12\n      task3_ee_disp: 0.21\n    result_rationale: >\n      Phase 2 worst tier: TSR 不恢复 (<18%), CAR 也部分丢失。两个维度都失败：\n      (1) TSR 恢复 minimal (9%→12%, vs baseline 75%）——SDF 训练在前 10K steps overwrite\n      了 task-critical representations。LoRA adapter 的有限 capacity（rank 8-16）在 SDF\n      阶段被重新配置为编码 avoidance behavior，后续 20K 纯 action loss 无法将这些\n      参数 reset 回 task-oriented configuration。模型收敛到错误的 basin——loss 值低但\n      task execution 路径已被 permanently disrupted。task1（chocolate_pudding）部分恢复\n      到 38%（从 36%）因为这是最简单的 task，其余 tasks 几乎无恢复。\n      (2) CAR 从 55.5% 降到 30%——safety encoding 不持久。去除 SDF loss 后，action loss\n      gradient 逐步 overwrite safety-relevant parameters，avoidance behavior 在 20K steps\n      内大幅退化。但 CAR 没完全回到 baseline 27%——残留了一些 structural bias。\n      (3) EE displacement 从 0.50m 降到 0.28m——模型介于 SDF aggressive avoidance 和\n      baseline natural movement 之间。\n      整体：Phase 2 模型严格劣于 LoRA-only（TSR 12% vs 35.5%, CAR 30% vs 50%）——\n      proof that SDF 训练造成不可逆损伤且 safety 也不 persist。\"two-phase strategy\"\n      升级路径彻底关闭。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Phase 2 Recovery Trajectory\"\n        columns: [\"Stage\", \"TSR (%)\", \"CAR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\", \"Fake Safe (%)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Pi0.5 baseline\", \"74.7\", \"26.8\", \"0.150\", \"98.2\"]\n          - [\"After 10K SDF (s2 l=0.005)\", \"9.0\", \"55.5\", \"0.505\", \"0\"]\n          - [\"After Phase 2 l=0 (worst)\", \"12.0\", \"30.0\", \"0.280\", \"22\"]\n          - [\"LoRA-only (for reference)\", \"35.5\", \"50.0\", \"0.280\", \"35\"]\n      - title: \"Phase 2 Per-Task Recovery\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"Base TSR (%)\", \"10K SDF TSR (%)\", \"Phase2 TSR (%)\", \"Recovered?\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"orange_juice\", \"64\", \"0\", \"4\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"chocolate_pudding\", \"86\", \"36\", \"38\", \"Marginal (task1 only)\"]\n          - [\"milk\", \"66\", \"0\", \"4\", \"No\"]\n          - [\"bbq_sauce\", \"76\", \"0\", \"2\", \"No\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Trajectory plot: TSR 和 CAR across 3 stages (baseline → SDF 10K → Phase 2 30K).\n        Both metrics first deteriorate then fail to recover. Annotate \"irreversible\n        damage zone\". Dashed line shows LoRA-only as counterfactual — strictly better\n        on both metrics.\n    analysis: >\n      Phase 2 确认 SDF 训练的双重破坏性：(1) task damage 不可逆——TSR 不恢复；(2) safety\n      不持久——CAR 在去除 SDF loss 后回落。Phase 2 模型在 TSR 和 CAR 上都严格劣于\n      LoRA-only，证明 SDF 训练 \"burned\" 了 LoRA capacity。这是最强 cautionary finding：\n      \"SDF auxiliary loss is a one-way door — it permanently degrades task ability,\n      and the safety it induces dissipates when the loss is removed. The model cannot\n      return to its pre-SDF state through continued training.\" 写入论文 Block 5 作为\n      \"why naive geometric supervision fails as a training strategy\"。\n\n  - name: \"spatial_bowl A1 Training Completion\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: \"Pi0.5 + LoRA + SDF (A1, l=0.005) on spatial_bowl 训练到 30K (已在 11K/30K)\"\n    expected_results:\n      final_loss: 0.0152\n      best_loss: 0.0138\n      best_step: 18000\n      steps_completed: 30000\n      training_stable: true\n      sdf_loss_component_at_30k: 0.0048\n      action_loss_component_at_30k: 0.0104\n      wall_time_hours: 34\n    result_rationale: >\n      spatial_bowl 的 SDF 训练比 object_pudding 更难——spatial tasks 中 bowl 位于\n      plate/ramekin/cabinet 等多个障碍物之间，obstacle geometry 更复杂，SDF gradient\n      方向更容易矛盾（推离一个障碍物可能推向另一个）。训练完成但 loss 高于 object_pudding\n      （0.0138 vs 0.0079-0.0117）。SDF loss component 占比 ~32%（vs object_pudding ~20%），\n      说明 geometric loss 与 action loss 在 spatial scene 下冲突更大。不 diverge 但\n      quality 较差。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      训练完成但 loss 偏高预示 eval 结果不理想。spatial scene 的多障碍物几何比\n      object_pudding 的单路径几何本质上更难 SDF optimize。\n\n  - name: \"spatial_bowl Eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: \"spatial_bowl A1 训练完成后 eval，验证 SDF 效果跨场景泛化\"\n    expected_results:\n      avg_TSR: 5\n      avg_CAR: 22\n      avg_max_ee_displacement_m: 0.35\n      fake_safe_pct: 8\n      n_episodes: 200\n      task0_TSR: 4\n      task0_CAR: 18\n      task0_ee_disp: 0.32\n      task1_TSR: 0\n      task1_CAR: 28\n      task1_ee_disp: 0.38\n      task2_TSR: 12\n      task2_CAR: 20\n      task2_ee_disp: 0.34\n      task3_TSR: 4\n      task3_CAR: 22\n      task3_ee_disp: 0.36\n      baseline_spatial_TSR: 57.5\n      baseline_spatial_CAR: 13\n      delta_CAR_over_baseline_pp: 9\n    result_rationale: >\n      spatial_bowl SDF CAR 仅 22%（baseline 13%，delta +9pp），远低于 object_pudding\n      的 +25pp 增量。原因：(1) spatial 场景中 bowl 被多个障碍物包围，EE-only SDF\n      gradient 在多障碍物场景下方向矛盾——推离 plate 可能推向 ramekin；(2) spatial tasks\n      的 arm body collision 比例更高（Claim 3 已证），EE-only avoidance 结构性不足；\n      (3) 训练 loss 更高说明 SDF 在 spatial 上学习质量更差。TSR=5% 与 object_pudding\n      一致——SDF 对 task performance 的破坏跨场景一致。但 CAR delta +9pp 在 200 episodes\n      下可能不 statistically significant（~18 episodes 差异），且可能被 LoRA-only 解释。\n      若 LoRA-only spatial 也有类似 CAR（需要额外实验但 worst tier 下合理假设），则\n      spatial_bowl 的 SDF effect = 0。scenes_with_sdf_effect 在严格意义下为 0（两个\n      场景的 SDF delta 都可被 LoRA capacity 解释）。\n    tables:\n      - title: \"Cross-Scene SDF Effect\"\n        columns: [\"Scene\", \"Base CAR (%)\", \"SDF CAR (%)\", \"Delta (pp)\", \"Base TSR (%)\", \"SDF TSR (%)\", \"TSR Cost (pp)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"object_pudding\", \"26.8\", \"52.5\", \"+25.7\", \"74.7\", \"6.8\", \"-67.9\"]\n          - [\"spatial_bowl\", \"13.0\", \"22.0\", \"+9.0\", \"57.5\", \"5.0\", \"-52.5\"]\n      - title: \"spatial_bowl Per-Task Detail\"\n        columns: [\"Task\", \"TSR (%)\", \"CAR (%)\", \"EE Disp (m)\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"pick_bowl_between_plate_ramekin\", \"4\", \"18\", \"0.32\"]\n          - [\"pick_bowl_on_ramekin\", \"0\", \"28\", \"0.38\"]\n          - [\"pick_bowl_on_stove\", \"12\", \"20\", \"0.34\"]\n          - [\"pick_bowl_on_cabinet\", \"4\", \"22\", \"0.36\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - >\n        Grouped bar: object_pudding vs spatial_bowl delta CAR (SDF over baseline).\n        object_pudding bar ~26pp, spatial_bowl bar ~9pp. Error bars on spatial\n        overlap with zero. Title: \"SDF Effect Does Not Generalize Across Scenes\"\n    analysis: >\n      spatial_bowl 结果严重削弱 Claim 4 泛化性。SDF 效果即使存在（object_pudding +26pp）\n      也是 scene-specific，在第二场景下 marginal (+9pp) 且可能不显著。结合 LoRA baseline\n      结果（SDF delta over LoRA ≈ 0），spatial_bowl 的 +9pp 也可能完全来自 LoRA。\n      scenes_with_sdf_effect = 0 (strict) or 1 (generous)。论文只能 claim \"SDF 效果\n      在最好情况下也 scene-specific 且 marginal\"。Cross-scene 泛化失败进一步支持\n      reframe 为 methodology paper——SDF 作为 method 不 generalizable。\n\n  - name: \"Lambda=0.1 Bracket Training\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: \"l=0.1 单 seed 训练，构建 4-point lambda 曲线\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"CANCELLED\"\n      cancellation_reason: \"LoRA baseline CAR ≈ SDF CAR, lambda dose-response curve 无科学价值\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      plan_009 的前提是 SDF 有 dose-dependent effect（更高 lambda → 更高 CAR）。但\n      LoRA baseline 结果（plan_003）表明 CAR ~50% 已是 LoRA capacity ceiling，SDF\n      不增加 CAR。lambda=0.1 只会进一步破坏 TSR（预期 ~2%）而 CAR 不会超过 50-55%。\n      34 GPU-hours 无科学回报。如果 reviewer 要求 lambda 曲线，已有数据足够构建 3-point\n      curve（lambda=0/LoRA, 0.005, 0.01）展示 \"CAR plateau, TSR monotonic decrease\"。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      取消是 worst tier 的必然结论。如果 SDF loss weight 不影响 CAR，增加 loss weight\n      只增加成本。资源释放给其他实验或节省。\n\n  - name: \"Lambda=0.1 Eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: \"Lambda=0.1 训练完成后 eval\"\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"CANCELLED\"\n      cancellation_reason: \"训练 (plan_009) 被取消\"\n    result_rationale: \"依赖 plan_009，同步取消。\"\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: \"N/A\"\n\n  - name: \"Full A1 Re-eval Decision\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: \"基于 plan_001 (50ep) 结果，决定是否需要 800ep full re-eval with fixed EE displacement script\"\n    expected_results:\n      decision: \"no_full_reeval_needed\"\n      ee_disp_confirms_obstacle_disp: true\n      confidence_from_50ep: \"high\"\n      variance_ee_disp_50ep: 0.004\n    result_rationale: >\n      50ep re-eval（plan_001）确认 EE displacement ≈ 0.018m，variance 极小（std ~0.004m），\n      与 800ep obstacle displacement 数据完全一致——robot 不动。不需要 800ep full re-eval：\n      (1) 50ep 的 EE displacement 分布已足够窄，统计 power 充分；(2) 800ep obstacle\n      displacement 已是 Claim 1 主力证据，EE displacement 只是补充验证；(3) 10 GPU-hours\n      在 worst tier 下无更好用途（plan_009 已取消，其他实验不需要该 GPU）。论文注释\n      \"EE displacement verified on 50-episode subset, consistent with 800-episode\n      obstacle displacement analysis\"。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      决定不做 full re-eval 是合理的 resource allocation。Claim 1 证据链已足够\n      （800ep obstacle disp + 50ep EE disp），更多数据不改变结论。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"982a4dde-eb2b-4839-9008-a1caec5118ff","total_cost_usd":1.0416115000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21342,"cache_read_input_tokens":43926,"output_tokens":34823,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21342,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":34686,"cache_read_input_tokens":32479,"cache_creation_input_tokens":310,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":310},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":15586,"outputTokens":17,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.015670999999999997,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":3,"outputTokens":34823,"cacheReadInputTokens":43926,"cacheCreationInputTokens":21342,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.0259405000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"35685fbb-d3f1-4664-b4ce-b32d51f618ee"}
